From: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu v13: keep the clock reference on a failed start

ipu_open() takes one gate_ipu reference (clk_prepare_enable) and
ipu_release() drops it. ipu_start() does not take one, but its error path
(a job that times out, or a bad route / buffer) called
clk_disable_unprepare(): every failed job dropped a reference the opener
still owns. After the first failure the IPU clock is gated (or the count
underflows) and every following job of the same opener times out too,
until the file is closed. Seen on the T33L (openimp #675: /proc clock tree
read gate_ipu at 0 MHz after IPU_START timeouts); the same code
is in this T32 tree (ingenic_ipu_v13.c:1006).

Keep the reference on the error path; open/release stay balanced.

Signed-off-by: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
---
--- a/drivers/video/ingenic_ipu/ingenic_ipu_v13.c	2026-11-20 22:21:02.479868404 +0100
+++ b/drivers/video/ingenic_ipu/ingenic_ipu_v13.c	2026-11-20 22:21:02.496868570 +0100
@@ -1003,7 +1003,8 @@
 err_ipu_set_bg_buffer:
 err_ipu_set_osd_chx_route:
 err_ipu_set_bg_route:
-	clk_disable_unprepare(ipu->clk);
+	/* the clock reference belongs to the open file (ipu_open / ipu_release):
+	 * dropping it here gated the IPU for every later job of this opener */
 err_cmd:
 	return ret;
 }
